s","value":"13"},{"name":"receivingYards","label":"Rec. Yards","value":"225"},{"name":"receivingTouchdowns","label":"Receiving Touchdowns","value":"1"},{"name":"yardsPerReception","label":"YDS/R","value":"17.3"}],"birthPlace":"Hudsonville, MI","draftText":"2025: Rd 3, Pk 70 (DET)"},"news":[{"headline":"Have skills, need opportunity: 10 fantasy football picks who just need a chance to shine","description":"Matt Bowen and Tristan H. Cockcroft list players they are most excited about, if and when opportunity knocks.","published":"2026-08-05T12:49:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/49517085/fantasy-football-sleepers-upside-picks-nfl-2026","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen and Tristan H. Cockcroft","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions WRs aiming to become NFL's best in 2026","description":"With Amon-Ra St. Brown setting the standard, the Lions' receivers are poised to push for elite status.","published":"2026-02-12T14:10:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/47902084/detroit-lions-amon-ra-st-brown-jameson-williams-isaac-teslaa-2026-outlook","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"36 NFL rookies on the 1 big lesson they learned this season","description":"Tyler Shough, Isaac TeSlaa and Jalon Walker were among the 36 rookies who learned how humbling and challenging the NFL can be.","published":"2025-12-26T11:31:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/47383983/nfl-rookies-tyler-shough-malaki-starks-cowboys-bears-packers","type":"Story","byline":"Sarah Barshop","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Best bets, DFS tips: Broncos inch closer to AFC West title, Lions stay in playoff hunt, Cowboys rebound?","description":"Betting the Christmas Day games? Here are the odds, game picks, prop plays and daily fantasy tips for all three.","published":"2025-12-24T14:03:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47402185/nfl-week-17-odds-lines-spread-betting-picks-dfs-tips-christmas-day-football-preview-cowboys-commanders-lions-vikings-broncos-chiefs","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colts' Jonathon Taylor leads Week 5 Madden NFL 26 ratings surge","description":"NFL players made major jumps with some losses in Madden NFL 26 ratings from Week 5.","published":"2025-10-10T19:49:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/gaming/story/_/id/46553664/madden-nfl-26-week-5-ratings-updates-jonathan-taylor-indianapolis-colts","type":"Story","byline":"Marco Wutz","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Don't be surprised if ... Charbonnet becomes an RB2, Johnston is on most-dropped list soon","description":"Will Charbonnet usurp Kenneth Walker III? Is Johnston a mirage? Is the Raiders' passing game underrated?","published":"2025-09-12T13:33:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/46224021/nfl-fantasy-football-rankings-predictions-surprises-week-2","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Karabell","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2025 Detroit Lions training camp: Latest intel, updates","description":"Follow our daily updates from Lions training camp, including intel as Detroit gears up for the 2025 season.","published":"2025-08-21T20:09:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/45704222/2025-nfl-training-camp-detroit-lions-updates-buzz-intel-position-battles","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions rookie Isaac TeSlaa has long been part of the Pride","description":"Rookie wide receiver Isaac TeSlaa, a third-round pick, is a Michigan native who was \"born to be a Lion.\"","published":"2025-05-17T10:00:04.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/45146975/detroit-lions-2025-draft-isaac-teslaa","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Detroit Lions 2025 NFL draft picks: Selection analysis","description":"Let's take a closer look at each of the Lions' 2025 draft picks.","published":"2025-04-26T23:23:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/44566938/detroit-lions-nfl-draft-picks-2025-selection-analysis-depth-chart","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2025 NFL draft: Louis Riddick's favorite prospects, sleepers","description":"Louis Riddick picks his guys in the 2025 class, including a hard-hitting safety, a ball-hawking corner and a bunch of offensive playmakers.","published":"2025-04-19T10:20:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2025/story/_/id/44687183/2025-nfl-draft-riddick-favorite-prospects-class-sleepers-ward-hunter-carter","type":"Story","byline":"Louis Riddick","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Isaac TeSlaa","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_TeSlaa","description":"American football player (born 2002)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:20Z","intro":"Isaac TeSlaa (teh-SLAH; born February 20, 2002) is an American professional football wide receiver for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Hillsdale Chargers and Arkansas Razorbacks. He was selected by the Lions in the third round of the 2025 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"TeSlaa is from Hudsonville, Michigan. His father, Mark, played college football as a wide receiver for the Hillsdale Chargers. TeSlaa grew up playing football as a quarterback and became a starter at Unity Christian High School as a junior. He led Unity Christian to the state championship that season, the first in school history. He then helped Unity Christian reach the state playoff semifinals in 2019, and that year he threw for 448 yards and 10 touchdowns while rushing for 1,139 yards and 14 touchdowns.\nIn addition to participating in football, TeSlaa also helped the basketball team to a state championship and competed in track and field, setting the school long jump record. He was lightly recruited and only had a single NCAA Division I offer, from the FCS-level Valparaiso Beacons. TeSlaa opted to sign with the Hillsdale Chargers, where his father and several other family members had attended."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"HILLSDALE\nTeSlaa became a wide receiver at Hillsdale and became a starter during his freshman season. In the COVID-19-shortened 2020–21 season, he caught five passes for 93 yards. He then led the team in the fall 2021 season with 45 receptions for 698 yards and seven touchdowns. He was named second-team All-Great Midwest Athletic Conference and placed third in the league in touchdown catches and fourth in receiving yards. In the 2022 season, he was one of the top NCAA Division II wide receivers, totaling 68 receptions for 1,325 yards and 13 touchdowns while being named the conference offensive player of the year. He was also named an honorable mention All-American and recorded seven games with at least 100 yards, finishing with an average of over 120 yards per game. He appeared in a total of 26 games in his tenure at Hillsdale, starting 24 of them and totaling 118 receptions for 2,116 yards and 19 touchdowns.\n\nARKANSAS\nTeSlaa transferred to the Arkansas Razorbacks following his third season at Hillsdale. He was the team's second-leading receiver during the 2023 season, recording 34 catches for 351 yards and two touchdowns. He returned for the 2024 season and recorded 28 receptions for 545 yards and three touchdowns, finishing his two-year stint with the Razorbacks having caught 62 passes for 896 yards and five touchdowns in 25 games played, 17 of which he started. He declared for the NFL draft after the season and was invited to the 2025 Senior Bowl.\n\nSTATISTICS"},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"TeSlaa was selected in the third round (70th overall) of the 2025 NFL draft by the Detroit Lions. He made his NFL debut in the season opener against the Green Bay Packers at Lambeau Field. TeSlaa recorded his first NFL reception and touchdown on a 13-yard one-handed diving catch from quarterback Jared Goff, reaching above his head to secure the pass before falling into the end zone. Despite the game being out of reach, the play gained attention and was ranked No. 19 on the NFL's Top 100 Plays of the 2025 NFL season. In the following week's game against the Chicago Bears, TeSlaa recorded his second career reception on a 29-yard one-handed diving catch. Both of his first two NFL receptions were one-handed catches, and each play was featured on the NFL's Top 100 Plays of the 2025 season, ranking No. 19 and No. 91, respectively. He earned his first professional start in Week 3 against the Baltimore Ravens. From Weeks 13 through 17, TeSlaa recorded a touchdown reception in four of five games. TeSlaa finished the season appearing in all 17 games, making three starts, and recorded 16 receptions for 239 yards and six touchdowns."}],"wikidataId":"Q132029855","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5123663","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/T/TeSlIs00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/isaac-teslaa/172430","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/isaac-teslaa/12430","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_TeSlaa"},"insights":["On the field for 48% of Detroit’s offensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.5M is the 27th-largest on the roster.","Under contract through 2028.","Drafted 70th overall in 2025 (round 3) by DET."]}